+# Build loading and unloading
+
+## The problem
+
+When a player joined, `Builds.server.luau` created their whole saved build in one frame. With
+20,000 blocks, each block was three instances (the `Part`, an `Owner` StringValue and a
+`PlacedAt` NumberValue). That's 60,000 instances, and each part was parented before its properties
+were set (`Instance.new("Part", parent)`), so every property change also went through the parented
+path. That was the ~2,100 ms `Script_Builds` frame. All 60,000 instances then reached clients in
+one burst, which caused the `Replicator ProcessPackets` hitch. On leave, the script read the
+children of the plot folder (60,000 instances) and destroyed all of it in one frame, which caused
+the smaller freeze.
+
+## What changed (`src/ServerScriptService/Builds.server.luau`)
+
+1. **Loading and unloading are spread over frames.** One job queue runs on `Heartbeat`. Each
+   frame it creates or destroys blocks until it has used `FRAME_BUDGET` (2 ms of server time) or
+   handled `MAX_BLOCKS_PER_FRAME` (250 blocks), whichever comes first. The budget is shared by all
+   plots, so eight players joining at once (for example on server start) cost no more per frame
+   than one. Jobs run in order. Unloads go to the front of the queue because they free plot slots
+   and memory.
+2. **One instance per block.** Owner and placed time moved out of child `StringValue` and
+   `NumberValue` instances into two server-side tables keyed by the part (`blockOwners`,
+   `blockPlacedAt`). A block is now one instance to create, replicate and destroy instead of
+   three. Placed time is still recorded for every block: loaded blocks keep the time from the save
+   and new blocks get `os.time()`.
+3. **Blocks are cloned from per-type templates.** Each clone gets its CFrame and is then parented,
+   so it replicates once with its final properties.
+4. **Removal owner check** now reads `blockOwners[part] == player.UserId`. It still allows only
+   the owner to remove a block, and only within reach. Parts this script didn't create have no
+   entry, so they can't be removed.
+5. **Plot slot lifecycle.** A leaving player's slot stays reserved until their blocks are fully
+   unloaded, so a new build can't load into cells that are still occupied. If all 8 slots are
+   taken at the moment someone joins (because a slot is still unloading), the join waits for a
+   slot to free up instead of failing with "no free plot". If a player leaves mid-load, their
+   remaining load is cancelled and what was already built is unloaded. The code also handles a
+   player leaving while `SavedBuilds.load` is yielding, for when it reads from a DataStore.
+
+Placing blocks (validation, rate limit, reach, occupied cells) works the same as before.
+
+## What players will notice
+
+- **No more server-wide freeze or rubber-banding** when a big build loads or unloads. Server
+  cost is capped at about 2 ms per frame.
+- **Builds appear over about 1.5 seconds** instead of all at once. A 20,000-block build at 250
+  blocks per frame takes about 80 frames. Saves are stored bottom layer first, so builds fill in
+  from the ground up. If several players join together, their builds load one after another, so
+  the last one in line can take several seconds to appear. Players can place blocks right away
+  while their build is still loading. If they place a block in a cell their save hasn't filled
+  yet, the new block wins and that saved block is skipped. Loading already skipped occupied cells
+  before this change.
+- **Builds disappear over about a second** when their owner leaves, instead of vanishing at once.
+- **Much smaller client hitches.** Clients get about 250 new parts per frame instead of 60,000
+  instances at once.
+- In rare cases a joining player may wait a moment for a plot while a departed player's build
+  finishes unloading. Before this change they got no plot at all.
+
+## Things to know
+
+- **Owner and placed time are no longer visible to clients.** Nothing on the client read them
+  before. If the upcoming placed-time feature needs the value on the client, add a remote that
+  returns `blockPlacedAt[part]` on request, or set it as an attribute on the part. An attribute
+  is cheaper than a child instance but still adds replication data to every block.
+- **Tuning:** raise `MAX_BLOCKS_PER_FRAME` and `FRAME_BUDGET` for faster loads, or lower them if
+  clients still hitch on low-end devices.
+- **Not changed:** a player who joins a full server still downloads every existing plot during
+  join (up to 7 × 20,000 parts). Turning on `Workspace.StreamingEnabled` would send clients only
+  the plots near them, which helps join time and client memory. That's a game-wide behavior change,
+  so it should be tested on its own.
+- **Not verified in Studio.** These changes have not been run in a live server or profiled. StyLua
+  and selene pass. Please take a new MicroProfiler capture with a 20,000-block build to confirm.
